        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update definitions of border width keywords]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43040</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43040"/>
        <updated>2026-02-06T20:07:22.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45496878?u=5fe01bc4df06a5bff99ef454943a6c0c8da2fd6c&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Updates the locations describing the border-width keyword values (thin, medium thick) to call out the values they correspond to, rather than the (old, no longer valid) claim that the values are not defined by the spec.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Theses values did start out without crisp equivalents, but in 2022 they were updated to have these specific definitions.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1227145898" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7254" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7254/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7254">w3c/csswg-drafts#7254</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">RESOLVED: thin, medium, and thick will be defined as 1px, 3px, and 5px respectively.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#border-width" rel="nofollow">https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#border-width</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The thin, medium, and thick keywords are equivalent to 1px, 3px, and 5px, respectively.</p>
</blockquote>]]></content>
