    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify discoverable credentials]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43039</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43039"/>
        <updated>2026-02-07T02:31:39.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">When writing <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Authentication/Passkeys" rel="nofollow">the passkeys guide</a> I didn't understand the discussion of discoverable versus non-discoverable credentials on MDN, and it was only by reading some other sources that I could make sense of it.</p>
<p dir="auto">In particular, the current doc says what a discoverable credential is, but not what a non-discoverable credential is, or what it is about ND credentials that makes them non-discoverable, or what the possible motivation for having ND credentials could be. Which makes the whole discussion mysterious: why not just make all credentials discoverable?</p>
<p dir="auto">There are also some errors (especially "means that the user can log in conveniently without having to supply credentials") that make things confusing.</p>
<p dir="auto">I thought it better to separate the underlying support and concepts (discoverable versus non-discoverable) from the application (autofill UI).</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>wbamberg</name>
            <email>wbamberg@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/wbamberg</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-02-06T18:52:10.000Z</published>
    </entry>
